        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-17T09:04:16Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(post): wrapped A on the Tormach microARC 4 (G93, cumulative A)\n\nThe PathPilot post no longer refuses an A that changes inside an\noperation. From the PathPilot Hub readings on #796 (A is linear degrees\nwith no rollover; G94 times a combined move by XYZ only; G93 is accepted\nand timed; an A-only F is deg/min):\n\n- A is posted cumulative (nearest equivalent of the held angle), bounded\n  by the stated travel, refused by name past it.\n- A feed that turns A and moves XYZ is G93: F = 1/t, t the longer of the\n  tip's path relative to the part at the programmed feed and the turn at\n  the stated A rate (rotaryRate, #885); floored, never rounded.\n- An A-only feed stays G94 in deg/min; G94 is restated before any other\n  motion and at each section end.\n- Turning moves are split until the tip stays within 0.005 mm of the\n  stream's segment; a machine with no A rate is refused by name.\n- The microARC 4 file states A max_normal_speed 360 deg/min (the Hub rate).\n\nFixes #796\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
