      },
      "message": "docs(guide): continuous 4-axis walkthrough on the Tormach 770MX + microARC 4\n\n\"Your first continuous 4-axis program\": a Rotary Parallel job on a round\nbar, from the machine file and the work offset on the A centreline to the\nposted program, read line by line (G93 on a move that turns A with X Y Z,\nA counting on past 180, the A rate cap, G94 back), what the post refuses,\na run in the PathPilot simulator and a single-block air cut.\n\nThe page ends with an air cut and tells the reader not to cut: Rotary\nParallel finishes the model's end faces to the axis, which on a bar held\nin a chuck is a cut through the bar (#2343). Rotary Offset is refused on\nthis machine file (#2344).\n\n- examples/first-continuous-4axis-part.camproj, .nc and the model, built\n  and held by crates/app/tests/continuous_4axis_part.rs (5 tests)\n- three pictures drawn from the example by\n  site/tools/first_continuous_4axis_pictures.py\n- site/tests/test_first_continuous_4axis_part.py holds the page to the\n  UI sources, the project, the program, the post and the pictures\n- continuous-4-axis.md and the Multi-axis index no longer say that no\n  post writes G93 or that tormach.cps indexes A only\n\nStacked on PR #2342 (#796).\n\nFixes #1904\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
